id: pm-26y269
title: Bound replication-gate Git work independently of tracker migration size
description: "Large audited tracker migrations cause changedLinesFromGit in surface-replication-gate.mjs to execute three git diff subprocesses for every changed path, even paths absent from all content-scoped replication triggers. The 1488-item closure-timestamp migration exposes roughly 9000 redundant Git subprocesses. Filter to declared content-trigger paths or batch patches while preserving deleted-file handling and fail-closed unknown evidence."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-19T09:04:56.152Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-19T09:15:14.861Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Git subprocess count is bounded by declared content triggers or a constant number of batched diffs, not unrelated changed tracker files; missing or unreadable diff evidence still activates applicable sets fail-closed; deleted structured triggers and unrelated-hunk negative controls remain covered; a large temporary Git fixture proves equivalent findings and bounded process work"
parent: pm-92if
risk: low
confidence: high
